# Portfolio development rules

## Project
- Hemayet's portfolio: Salesforce, AI agents, and engineering projects.
- Use the versions installed in package-lock.json.
- Follow AGENTS.md and read relevant bundled Next.js documentation
  in node_modules/next/dist/docs before changing framework code.

## Structure
- Routes and layouts: src/app/
- Components: src/components/[component-name]/[ComponentName].tsx
- Shared types: src/types/index.ts
- Constants and utilities: src/utils/
- Import alias: @/* maps to src/*
- Keep public assets and configuration files at the project root.

## Code
- Use strict TypeScript; avoid any and import types with import type.
- Use PascalCase for components and camelCase for functions.
- Use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for shared constants.
- Add 'use client' only when client-side functionality requires it.
- Use next/link for internal navigation.
- Use Tailwind utilities and responsive layouts.
- Preserve semantic HTML, keyboard access, and visible focus styles.
- Keep secrets out of source code and Git.

## Content
- Use verified facts and contact links.
- Identify simulations and fictional companies clearly.
- Do not present planned or unfinished work as completed delivery.
- Describe projects through problem, solution, technology, and evidence.
- Keep placeholder content clearly labeled until replaced.

## Verification
- Run npm run lint and npm run build after code changes.
- Check affected routes and links in the browser.
- Check mobile layouts when changing the UI.
- Add meaningful tests for new behavior when appropriate.
- Do not add dependencies or change configuration without a concrete need.

## Git
- Inspect the diff before committing.
- Use descriptive commits such as feat:, fix:, docs:, or chore:.
- Never commit node_modules, .next, credentials, or private environment files.
